## Section 2 — The DevOps Profession (8 pts)

### 2.1 Table (4 pts)

| Role | Main goal | One daily task | One tool |
|---|---|---|---|
| DevOps Engineer | Speed up and automate the path from code to production | Fixing/improving a CI/CD pipeline step | Jenkins / GitHub Actions |
| SRE | Keep production reliable within agreed error budgets | Reviewing alerts/dashboards and on-call triage | Prometheus / Grafana |
| Sysadmin | Keep servers and infrastructure running day-to-day | Patching servers, managing user accounts/permissions | Ansible / Bash |
| Platform Engineer | Build internal tools/platforms so other devs can self-serve | Improving an internal developer platform (IDP) or golden path template | Backstage / Terraform |

### 2.2 Five specific skills to work on (3 pts)

1. Writing a systemd unit file from scratch (and using `systemctl` to manage it).
2. Writing a multi-stage Dockerfile that minimizes final image size.
3. Writing a GitHub Actions/GitLab CI YAML pipeline with build, test, and deploy stages.
4. Writing a Terraform module to provision a VPC + EC2 instance from scratch.
5. Writing a bash script that handles `set -euo pipefail`, argument parsing, and error trapping properly.

### 2.3 Not responsible for (1 pt)

A DevOps engineer is not responsible for writing the business logic/features of the application — that's owned by the software development team (product engineers).

